<title>USA: USDA sets crop report, supply-demand report dates.</title>
<headline>USDA sets crop report, supply-demand report dates.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department announced Wednesday the dates for release of its monthly crop reports and supply-demand estimates during 1997.</p>
<p>Both reports will be released on the same dates except in January. Release time will be 0830 Eastern in all cases.</p>
<p>In January, the crop report will be January 9. Supply-demand report will be January 10 along with the annual crop report, winter wheat seedings and grain stocks reports.</p>
<p>Schedule for the rest of the year is February 12, March 11, April 11, May 12, June 12, July 11, August 12, September 12, October 10, November 10 and December 11.</p>
</text>
